how do you overcome the fear of  rejection I'm going to answer that  question in today's episode of ask Evan  so recent asks a question for one of my  YouTube fans love you guys  Sanjaya who wrote in this a amazing  video Evan thanks Angela  I would like to get advice about fear of  rejection because most of the people  have this mindset so there's a fantastic  question and one that I think a lot of  entrepreneurs go through how to overcome  that fear of rejection I'm gonna share  with you my three tips on how to do it  number one is feel the fear and do it  anyway so what I want you to understand  is you can't get rid of that fear I  don't want you to think about how do I  completely get rid of that fear because  fear is natural fear is normal and a lot  of people they think because they're  afraid of it then they're not going to  do it so your first starting point is  understanding that it's natural to be  afraid of rejection and you don't want  to let that fear hold you back you want  to be motivated by the fear you want to  not make a decision because you're  afraid of it you know if there's an  opportunity in front of you the reason  not to do it should be something logical  something rational not because you're  afraid to do it so it's understanding  that it's okay to be afraid  feel that fear and do it anyway number  two is believe that you can help them  this is one of the biggest things that  helped me early on in my career when I  was being approached by brands who  wanted to work with me and one of the  first companies that I work with was  Microsoft and they reached out to me  said every can you help us with this  campaign that we're doing and I was so  afraid at that time because I thought  Who am I like I'm this I mean I'm  nothing compared to Microsoft what value  can I possibly give them  and I was so worried they would walk  away from the deal and they wouldn't  want to work with me and then I realized  that hey I can actually help these guys  right the value that I bring is  substantial and they're coming to me for  a reason and so this has helped me over  and over and over in my career whenever  I felt nervous or afraid or thought I  might get rejection it's not going into  a situation trying to sell somebody  something it's knowing that you really  can help them so it's believing in your  product or service and knowing that it  can actually have  really positive impact on their lives I  found that that really reduce the amount  of fear for me going into that situation  number three is change your approach I'm  a big believer in betting on your  strengths and doing things that you're  really really good at and want to learn  and not try to improve your weaknesses  and doing the stuff that you suck at and  hate because that's never the path to  build a highly successful company or for  you to be happy right if you're forcing  yourself to do stuff that you don't like  over and over and over again you're  never going to build something great or  be a happy person with your life right  and so what's causing this fear of  rejection so for example if you are  doing cold calling and you hate cold  calling and every time you look at the  phone you're looking at and say I don't  want to pick up that phone cold calling  can work and it works for some people  but it may not work for you and the  right approach may be to change your  strategy do something else that's more  comfortable for you that you excel at  that you want to be better at that  you're more passionate about and so if  you're looking at something and you're  constantly afraid of it and constantly  thinking I don't I really won't want to  do that again think is the reason I  don't want to do because you're just  afraid of it or because there's a  logical reason behind it and sometimes  the solution is just a change your  approach and do something that's best  fit for you  focus on your strengths and not your  weaknesses so remember feel the fear and  do 